---
import { site } from "../site";

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "What is send0?",
    a: `An email API where the inbox is the main object. One API call gives an agent a real address that can send, receive and thread replies, and tells your code about new mail through webhooks, live streams or a long-poll <code>wait</code> call. It's open source, and you can use our cloud or run it yourself.`,
  },
  {
    q: "How is it different from a transactional email API?",
    a: `Transactional APIs are built to send receipts and password resets. Receiving is usually an add-on that forwards raw mail to a webhook. send0 starts from the inbox: messages are parsed, threaded, authenticated and stored, codes and links are extracted, and your agent can reply in the same thread. It also sends, so many teams won't need a second provider.`,
  },
  {
    q: "When does the beta open?",
    a: `Soon. Join the waitlist and we'll email you once when the beta opens, with no newsletters in between. ${site.repoPublic ? `You can follow progress on <a href="${site.github}">GitHub</a> in the meantime.` : "The source code opens at the same time."}`,
  },
  {
    q: "Will sites block send0.email addresses as disposable?",
    a: `We work hard to make sure they don't. Every send0.email inbox belongs to a signed-in account, we never market it as throwaway mail, and test inboxes live on a separate sandbox domain. For anything critical, paid plans let you use your own domain.`,
  },
  {
    q: "Will mail from my agent land in the inbox?",
    a: `send0 sends through Amazon SES with SPF, DKIM and DMARC aligned, sets proper threading headers, and suppresses bounced or complaining addresses automatically. The strict limits on free accounts exist to keep the shared domain's reputation high for everyone. For real volume, use your own domain.`,
  },
  {
    q: "Can I use send0 for cold outreach or newsletters?",
    a: `No. Unsolicited outreach, bulk mail and marketing sends are against our <a href="/acceptable-use">acceptable use policy</a>, and accounts that try are suspended. send0 is for conversations people start or expect.`,
  },
  {
    q: "How do you keep agents safe from malicious email?",
    a: `Every inbound message includes SPF, DKIM and DMARC results, a spam score and a prompt-injection flag. You can drop unauthenticated mail per inbox, set allowlists and blocklists, and require human approval before anything is sent. The MCP server passes message bodies to the model as data, not as instructions.`,
  },
  {
    q: "What does AGPL-3.0 mean for me?",
    a: `If you call send0's API from your app, open source or not, the AGPL puts no obligations on your code. If you modify the send0 server itself and let others use it over a network, you have to publish those changes under the same license. The SDKs and MCP server are MIT, so you can embed them anywhere.`,
  },
  {
    q: "Can I self-host send0 commercially?",
    a: `Yes. Run it inside your company, for your own products, at any scale. The AGPL only asks that you share changes you make to the server if you offer it to others as a service.`,
  },
  {
    q: "What does self-hosting need?",
    a: `A server that runs Docker, Postgres, S3-compatible storage such as MinIO, and a way to send, either Amazon SES or any SMTP relay. Receiving needs port 25 open, or you can forward mail from Cloudflare Email Routing to your instance.`,
  },
];
---

<section class="section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="layout">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">FAQ</span>
      <h2 id="faq-title" class="h2">
        Questions, <span class="dim">answered.</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Something missing? Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email.hello}`}>{site.email.hello}</a> and you'll get a reply from a person.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="list reveal">
      {faqs.map((f, i) => (
        <details name="faq" open={i === 0}>
          <summary>
            <span>{f.q}</span>
            <span class="plus" aria-hidden="true" />
          </summary>
          <div class="answer" set:html={f.a} />
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .layout {
    display: grid;
    gap: 40px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 1000px) {
    .layout {
      grid-template-columns: 0.8fr 1.2fr;
      gap: 56px;
      align-items: start;
    }
    .layout .section-head {
      position: sticky;
      top: 100px;
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }
  }
  .lede a,
  .answer :global(a) {
    color: var(--fg);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    text-decoration-color: var(--border-strong);
  }
  .lede a:hover,
  .answer :global(a:hover) {
    text-decoration-color: var(--accent);
  }
  .list {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  summary {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 24px;
    padding: 22px 0;
    font-size: 17px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }
  summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  summary:hover {
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .plus {
    position: relative;
    flex: none;
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
  }
  .plus::before,
  .plus::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    margin: auto;
    background: var(--fg-muted);
    transition: transform 0.2s ease;
  }
  .plus::before {
    width: 14px;
    height: 1.5px;
  }
  .plus::after {
    width: 1.5px;
    height: 14px;
  }
  details[open] .plus::after {
    transform: rotate(90deg);
  }
  .answer {
    padding: 0 40px 24px 0;
    font-size: 15.5px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }
  .answer :global(code) {
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
</style>
